        "original_id": "10558575-3cc7-5539-8323-8e914eacadf3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Arundel Castle, Sussex, Norfolk\n- People: Duke of Norfolk\n- Events: English Civil War\n- Concepts: Parliamentarians, Royalists\n\nFacts:\n- The English Civil War lasted from 1642 to 1651 and consisted of armed conflicts and political struggles over the governance of England between Parliamentarians, also called Roundheads, and Royalists, also called Cavaliers.\n- Arundel Castle was damaged during the English Civil War.\n- Arundel Castle was restored in the 18th and 19th centuries.\n- Arundel Castle in Sussex is the seat of the Duke of Norfolk.\n- The title Duke of Norfolk refers to the county of Norfolk, although the seat is Arundel Castle in Sussex.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
